insert into public.piece (id, sku, date_cataloged, item_type_code, description, primary_materials, size_length, maker_id, tier_code, condition, repair_needed, existing_tag_price, asking_price, photo_taken, listing_status, photo_file_note, verification_note, group_lot_note, condition_detail, repair_check_detail, notes, source, original_ref, created_at, updated_at) values ('53','NK-005','2026-07-24','NK','European-style charm bead necklace - gold-tone snake chain with threaded barrel clasp holding approx. a dozen large-hole charm beads: pale pink glass/stone rondelles, cream mother-of-pearl discs, black onyx-style wedges, faceted blush crystal, pink pave rhinestone rondelle, and several ornate silver-tone floral and heart-motif metal beads','Gold-tone plated base metal chain; mixed charm beads - glass, mother-of-pearl, black stone, rhinestone, silver-tone metal','~17-18in','2','B','Needs Repair','f',NULL,NULL,'t','Not Listed','IMG_2489-IMG_2492','CHECK EVERY METAL BEAD FOR A HALLMARK (ALE 925, Chamilia, Trollbeads). Branded beads have real individual resale value; generic ones are worth a few dollars',NULL,'Fair to good - NOTICEABLE plating wear on chain and clasp; some silver beads darkened','None structural; confirm threaded clasp screws fully closed','DO NOT DISASSEMBLE before checking stamps - may be worth more parted out than whole. Chain condition caps the price of the piece as a unit | Provisional tier: B pending - C if beads are branded sterling','Catalog Session 2026-07-24','was SW-033','2026-07-24 16:14:39.504067+00','2026-07-24 16:14:39.504067+00');
insert into public.piece (id, sku, date_cataloged, item_type_code, description, primary_materials, size_length, maker_id, tier_code, condition, repair_needed, existing_tag_price, asking_price, photo_taken, listing_status, photo_file_note, verification_note, group_lot_note, condition_detail, repair_check_detail, notes, source, original_ref, created_at, updated_at) values ('54','NK-006','2026-07-24','NK','Fine gold-tone chain with wire-linked front section - small white pearls individually wire-wrapped between chain links, with five black teardrop briolettes suspended as graduated drops across the front; small barrel or magnetic clasp','Gold-tone or gold-filled fine chain and wire (verify); small white pearls (cultured or glass - verify); black onyx or black glass teardrops','~17-18in','2','B','Excellent','f',NULL,NULL,'t','Not Listed','IMG_2499 / IMG_2500','THREE CHECKS: pearls cultured vs. glass; drops onyx vs. glass; chain gold-filled vs. plated (GF / 14-20 stamp)',NULL,'Very good - chain bright, no visible kinks or stretched links','Inspect the wire wraps on each drop - fine-gauge loops are the failure point','Most refined piece in the batch - fine gauge, restrained, everyday-wearable. Skilled consistent wire wrapping | Provisional tier: B - C if two of three materials verify real','Catalog Session 2026-07-24','was SW-039','2026-07-24 16:14:39.504067+00','2026-07-24 16:14:39.504067+00');
insert into public.piece (id, sku, date_cataloged, item_type_code, description, primary_materials, size_length, maker_id, tier_code, condition, repair_needed, existing_tag_price, asking_price, photo_taken, listing_status, photo_file_note, verification_note, group_lot_note, condition_detail, repair_check_detail, notes, source, original_ref, created_at, updated_at) values ('55','NK-007','2026-07-24','NK','Triple-strand torsade - three twisted strands of small faceted black rondelles punctuated by gold-tone filigree ball beads; large polished AMMONITE FOSSIL pendant (natural exterior on one face, cut and polished spiral cross-section on the reverse) set in a gold-tone bail; ornate gold-tone floral three-hole end connectors and lobster clasp','Black onyx or black glass rondelles (verify); ammonite fossil (calcite-replaced shell); gold-tone base metal findings','~18-20in','2','C','Excellent','f','100.00',NULL,'t','Not Listed','IMG_2501-IMG_2504, IMG_2512','Onyx vs. glass - test with NK-001 and BR-027. Pendant ID now settled (ammonite, not druzy).','Black bead verification group','Very good - findings bright, no visible losses','Confirm all three strands are secure in both end connectors','HIGHEST TAG IN THE BATCH and the material now justifies it. Comp: ''ammonite fossil necklace'', ''ammonite pendant'' - NOT druzy. Reaches fossil and natural-history collectors as well as jewelry buyers. PHOTOGRAPH THE POLISHED SPIRAL FACE - that is the selling image. Commercially cut slices this size and colour are overwhelmingly Madagascar material, Cretaceous, roughly 110 million years old; phrase as ''Madagascar-type ammonite'' rather than stating origin as fact. Strongest story attached to any piece in this batch. Entry revised 24 Jul 2026 after additional photo IMG_2512.','Catalog Session 2026-07-24','was SW-040','2026-07-24 16:14:39.504067+00','2026-07-24 16:14:39.504067+00');
insert into public.piece (id, sku, date_cataloged, item_type_code, description, primary_materials, size_length, maker_id, tier_code, condition, repair_needed, existing_tag_price, asking_price, photo_taken, listing_status, photo_file_note, verification_note, group_lot_note, condition_detail, repair_check_detail, notes, source, original_ref, created_at, updated_at) values ('56','NK-008','2026-07-24','NK','Station necklace - gold-tone chain of alternating twisted bar links and round links, with five faceted smoky quartz rounds spaced around the lower half, each stone wire-linked into the chain; textured lobster clasp in a contrasting silver/white tone','Smoky quartz; gold-tone chain (verify for gold-fill); silver-tone clasp','~17-18in','2','B','Excellent','f',NULL,NULL,'t','Not Listed','IMG_2509-IMG_2511','Chain and end links for ''GF'' or ''14/20'' - gold-fill stays bright the way this has',NULL,'Very good - chain bright throughout, no visible plating loss','None apparent; check the wire loop at each stone','Clasp is a mismatched replacement (silver on gold) - easy upgrade if you want to lift the piece | Provisional tier: B - C if the chain is gold-filled','Catalog Session 2026-07-24','was SW-043','2026-07-24 16:14:39.504067+00','2026-07-24 16:14:39.504067+00');
insert into public.piece (id, sku, date_cataloged, item_type_code, description, primary_materials, size_length, maker_id, tier_code, condition, repair_needed, existing_tag_price, asking_price, photo_taken, listing_status, photo_file_note, verification_note, group_lot_note, condition_detail, repair_check_detail, notes, source, original_ref, created_at, updated_at) values ('57','NK-009','2026-07-24','NK','Gold-tone cable chain hung with approximately fourteen faceted baroque/pendalogue crystal drops in ruby red and amber yellow, each suspended on its own jump ring across the front of the chain','Faceted glass crystal (chandelier-prism style drops); gold-tone base metal chain and jump rings',NULL,'2','A','Excellent','f','35.00',NULL,'t','Not Listed','IMG_2520 / IMG_2521','Confirm Sally vs. buyout','Glass bundle candidate','Very good - drops bright and unchipped, chain clean','Check each jump ring is fully closed - drops are hung individually','Chandelier prism drops used as jewelry - a recognized, searchable style. GLASS not gemstone. Photographs well above its tier; red-and-amber against gold is the most striking colour combination in the batch','Catalog Session 2026-07-24','was SW-048','2026-07-24 16:16:25.187781+00','2026-07-24 16:16:25.187781+00');
